  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Medline Industries has $806M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Medline Industries received 678 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.2M, and obligations are up 39.2% year over year. Obligations have risen each reported fiscal year: $262M in FY21, $281M in FY22, $337M in FY23, $370M in FY24, $579M in FY25, and $806M in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is by far the largest buyer, obligating $763M. The largest market category is Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers with $769M in obligations. Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing follow with $35.8M and $916K respectively. FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial. This picture shows where federal demand is concentrated and which product categories and agencies account for the bulk of Medline Industries' federal business this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Medline Industries' top federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer, obligating $763M. The Department of Health and Human Services obligates $32M and the Department of Justice obligates $10M. Smaller obligations come from the Department of the Treasury ($295K), the Department of the Interior ($109K), and the Department of Defense ($63.1K)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product markets drive Medline Industries' federal obligations?",
        "body": "Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is the largest market with $769M in obligations. Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing accounts for $35.8M, and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing accounts for $916K. Other listed markets include In-Vitro Diagnostic Substance Manufacturing ($173K) and several smaller categories."
      }
    ]
  },
